#4471 was filed as one bug: dates parse month first in eu locales. The reports hold two
different problems. Only the first is the parser.

<Callout>
One ticket hid two bugs. Fixing the parser will not stop the form.
</Callout>

## The split

<ProblemSplit ticket={4471} />

## Problems

1. **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first, so day-first tenants get
   flipped dates (7 April → 4 July). 379 reports. Five of them read as a one-day move
   (`desk-notes.json`); they are counted here, where they are filed.
2. **`hint`**: tenants on the `booking-v3` form (`alder.physio`, `copper.studio`,
   `pale.harbour`) see `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field. Their people type month first and
   the form reads it their way. 33 reports. The parser fix does not touch this.

379 + 33 = 412. Intake's `intakeTag` is a guess from the browser; we placed each report by its
tenant's locale and booking form, and removed 15 repeated rows (one id, one report).

